cture: This is a two-column, 21-row technical specification table for the Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0. The left column lists specification parameters, and the right column gives the corresponding values, units, conditions, and compliance details. There is no separate header row, but the implied headers are Specification and Value. The rows are organized into operational performance, utilities and environment, physical characteristics, control/monitoring, and conformity. Superscripts in the table connect to footnotes in the surrounding context: footnote 1 defines standby, footnote 2 points to battery limits and the Owner's Manual, footnotes 3 and 4 reference Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU and Pressure Equipment (Safety) Regulations 2016, and footnote 5 limits ETL recognition to recognized electrolyser versions. The surrounding context identifies the product as Enapter's patented anion exchange membrane electrolyser, a standardised, stackable, flexible system for on-site hydrogen production with advanced software integration and remote control.\n\nKey data points and patterns: Production rate is up to 500 NL/h, up to 1.0785 kg/24 h, equivalent to 0.5 Nm3/h. Hydrogen purity depends on output pressure: at 35 barg, purity is 99.9% with less than 1,000 ppm H2O and less than 5 ppm O2 at 25 °C; at 8 barg, purity is 98.8% with less than 12,000 ppm H2O and less than 5 ppm O2 at 25 °C. Output pressure is up to 35 barg. Nominal power consumption is 4.8 kWh/Nm3 of H2 produced at beginning of life, which is consistent with the operative power consumption of 2.4 kW at beginning of life if the unit produces about 0.5 Nm3/h. Peak power consumption is 3 kW. Heat dissipation is 0.6 kW at beginning of life and maximum heat dissipation is 0.9 kW at end of life. Standby power consumption is 0.3 kW. Power supply is 220–240 V AC, 50/60 Hz. Water requirements include minimum ASTM D1193-06 Type IV or recommended Type II or Type III water, water consumption of approximately 420 m